{
  "sutta_id": "SN15.10",
  "verses": [
    {
      "number": 1,
      "pali": "Saṁyutta Nikāya 15.10 ",
      "english": "Linked Discourses 15.10 "
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "pali": "1. Paṭhamavagga ",
      "english": "Chapter One "
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "pali": "Puggalasutta ",
      "english": "A Single Individual "
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "pali": "Ekaṁ samayaṁ bhagavā rājagahe viharati gijjhakūṭe pabbate. ",
      "english": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha, on the Vulture’s Peak Mountain. "
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "pali": "Tatra kho bhagavā bhikkhū āmantesi: ",
      "english": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, "
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "pali": "“bhikkhavo”ti. ",
      "english": "“Mendicants!” "
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "pali": "“Bhadante”ti te bhikkhū bhagavato paccassosuṁ. ",
      "english": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. "
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "pali": "Bhagavā etadavoca: ",
      "english": "The Buddha said this: "
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "pali": "“Anamataggoyaṁ, bhikkhave, saṁsāro …pe… ",
      "english": "“Mendicants, this transmigration has no known beginning. … "
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "pali": "ekapuggalassa, bhikkhave, kappaṁ sandhāvato saṁsarato siyā evaṁ mahā aṭṭhikaṅkalo aṭṭhipuñjo aṭṭhirāsi yathāyaṁ vepullo pabbato, sace saṁhārako assa, sambhatañca na vinasseyya. ",
      "english": "One individual roaming and transmigrating for an eon would amass a heap of bones the size of this Mount Vepulla, if they were gathered together and not lost. "
    },
    {
      "number": 11,
      "pali": "Taṁ kissa hetu? ",
      "english": "Why is that? "
    },
    {
      "number": 12,
      "pali": "Anamataggoyaṁ, bhikkhave, saṁsāro …pe… ",
      "english": "This transmigration has no known beginning. … "
    },
    {
      "number": 13,
      "pali": "alaṁ vimuccitun”ti. ",
      "english": "This is quite enough for you to become disillusioned, dispassionate, and freed regarding all conditions.” "
    },
    {
      "number": 14,
      "pali": "Idamavoca bhagavā. ",
      "english": "That is what the Buddha said. "
    },
    {
      "number": 15,
      "pali": "Idaṁ vatvāna sugato athāparaṁ etadavoca satthā: ",
      "english": "Then the Holy One, the Teacher, went on to say: "
    },
    {
      "number": 16,
      "pali": "“Ekassekena kappena, ",
      "english": "“If the bones of a single individual "
    },
    {
      "number": 17,
      "pali": "puggalassaṭṭhisañcayo; ",
      "english": "for a single eon were gathered up, "
    },
    {
      "number": 18,
      "pali": "Siyā pabbatasamo rāsi, ",
      "english": "they’d make a pile the size of a mountain: "
    },
    {
      "number": 19,
      "pali": "iti vuttaṁ mahesinā. ",
      "english": "so said the great seer. "
    },
    {
      "number": 20,
      "pali": "So kho panāyaṁ akkhāto, ",
      "english": "And this is declared to be "
    },
    {
      "number": 21,
      "pali": "vepullo pabbato mahā; ",
      "english": "as huge as Mount Vepulla, "
    },
    {
      "number": 22,
      "pali": "Uttaro gijjhakūṭassa, ",
      "english": "higher than the Vulture’s Peak "
    },
    {
      "number": 23,
      "pali": "magadhānaṁ giribbaje. ",
      "english": "in the Magadhan mountain range. "
    },
    {
      "number": 24,
      "pali": "Yato ca ariyasaccāni, ",
      "english": "But then, with right understanding, "
    },
    {
      "number": 25,
      "pali": "sammappaññāya passati; ",
      "english": "one sees the noble truths—"
    },
    {
      "number": 26,
      "pali": "Dukkhaṁ dukkhasamuppādaṁ, ",
      "english": "suffering, suffering’s origin, "
    },
    {
      "number": 27,
      "pali": "dukkhassa ca atikkamaṁ; ",
      "english": "suffering’s transcendence, "
    },
    {
      "number": 28,
      "pali": "Ariyaṁ caṭṭhaṅgikaṁ maggaṁ, ",
      "english": "and the noble eightfold path "
    },
    {
      "number": 29,
      "pali": "dukkhūpasamagāminaṁ. ",
      "english": "that leads to the stilling of suffering. "
    },
    {
      "number": 30,
      "pali": "Sa sattakkhattuṁparamaṁ, ",
      "english": "After roaming on seven times at most, "
    },
    {
      "number": 31,
      "pali": "sandhāvitvāna puggalo; ",
      "english": "that individual "
    },
    {
      "number": 32,
      "pali": "Dukkhassantakaro hoti, ",
      "english": "makes an end of suffering, "
    },
    {
      "number": 33,
      "pali": "sabbasaṁyojanakkhayā”ti. ",
      "english": "with the ending of all fetters.” "
    },
    {
      "number": 34,
      "pali": "Dasamaṁ. ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 35,
      "pali": "Paṭhamo vaggo. ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 36,
      "pali": "Tassuddānaṁ ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 37,
      "pali": "Tiṇakaṭṭhañca pathavī, ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 38,
      "pali": "assu khīrañca pabbataṁ; ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 39,
      "pali": "Sāsapā sāvakā gaṅgā, ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 40,
      "pali": "daṇḍo ca puggalena cāti. ",
      "english": ""
    }
  ]
}